  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABIfYmOg",
      "title": "compliance: add Compliance Module specs",
      "author": "0xiamflux",
      "number": 971,
      "body": "## Context\r\n\r\nAn OP Stack chain has no way to condition value crossing its canonical bridge where it cannot be\r\nbypassed. Screening at the sequencer misses deposits submitted to L1, which carry forced inclusion,\r\nand it misses withdrawals, which finalize on L1. \r\n\r\nThese specs describe an optional hook that performs screening. The `OptimismPortal` gains one optional hook\r\naddress. While it is `address(0)`, OP stack default behavior remains unchanged. When set, the Portal offers every\r\nitem to the hook before value reaches its recipient. The hook answers proceed, hold or reject, and a held item\r\nexecutes later on the terms the Portal committed to.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\nNew pages:\r\n\r\n- `specs/experimental/compliance/overview.md`\r\n- `specs/experimental/compliance/optimism-portal.md`\r\n- `specs/experimental/compliance/l1-standard-bridge.md`\r\n- `specs/experimental/compliance/policy.md`\r\n- `specs/experimental/contracts/L1/compliance-module.md`\r\n\r\nChains that set no hook are unaffected.\r\n\r\nCloses [#732](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism-private/issues/732)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-14T21:25:08Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-09T14:57:50Z",
      "additions": 1719,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABKBxjaQ",
      "title": "compliance: spec improvements from fma",
      "author": "0xOneTony",
      "number": 977,
      "body": "Spec fixes from the bridge hook FMA review, on top of #971, grouped by failure mode.\r\n\r\n**FM2: Completions publish more deposit gas than one L2 block can take**\r\n- The published deposit gas count covers the whole L1 block in which a hook is set or removed.\r\n\r\n**FM3: A withdrawal calls the hook or the bridge's escrow functions**\r\n- `completeWithdrawalTransaction` reverts if the target is an Unsafe Target at the time of completion.\r\n\r\n**FM9: The policy screens the wrong parties**\r\n- The policy always receives two parties, sender then recipient, decoded only from messages the messengers sent.\r\n- The module reads the L1 bridge and messenger addresses from the Portal's `SystemConfig` when deployed.\r\n- New `parties()` view returns the same two addresses.\r\n\r\n**FM10: A clearance outlives the check it was written for**\r\n- Completion passes the policy the record's `clearedAt`.\r\n\r\n**FM12 / FM17: A compromised policy / a wrong disable cutoff**\r\n- `setPolicy`, `disable` and `enable` emit `PolicySet`, `Disabled` (with the cutoff) and `Enabled`.\r\n\r\n**FM13: The module's balance stops covering what it holds**\r\n- The bridge moves held tokens before the hook records the hold.\r\n\r\n**FM15: Non-standard tokens break holds or completions**\r\n- The module supports ETH, Native L1 Tokens and `OptimismMintableERC20` tokens.\r\n\r\n**FM19: The hook stands between governance and L2**\r\n- `depositTransaction` skips the hook for deposits sent by the ProxyAdmin owner, so governance actions on L2 never wait on screening. The overview's goals note the exception.\r\n\r\nCloses https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism-private/issues/823",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T13:08:54Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 1588,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABIT42BA",
      "title": "deposits: Split fork amendments into per-fork pages",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 969,
      "body": "Makes `deposits.md` describe the Bedrock behaviour only, and moves each fork's deposit changes into a per-fork `deposits.md` page.\n\n- `deposits.md` now states the Bedrock state with no fork-gating. Each rule a later fork changes carries a \"Changed by <fork>\" note linking to that fork's page.\n- Each fork that changes deposit rules has a `deposits.md`: Regolith, Canyon, Ecotone, Isthmus, Jovian, Karst, and Lagoon.\n- The Regolith and Canyon overview pages now link to their `deposits.md`.\n\nThe fork-amendments index should be completed once this lands, so the whole spec is self-consistent and canonical.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-14T03:52:07Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 830,
      "deletions": 650
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABHPP7hQ",
      "title": "interop: specify per-message expiry and SuperchainETHBridge refunds",
      "author": "karlfloersch",
      "number": 960,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nSpecifies per-message interop expiry and `SuperchainETHBridge` refunds, implemented in ethereum-optimism/optimism#23259.\n\nA destination chain's sequencer can refuse to relay an interop message forever, and executing messages cannot be included through deposits. Once the expiry window passes, the message can never be relayed. This specifies how the source chain learns that, using only a withdrawal and a deposit, so applications can undo the send.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **New `interop/message-expiry.md`:**\n  - the flow (export on the destination, relay through L1, expire on the source);\n  - `L1CrossDomainMessenger.relayUndeliveredMessage`;\n  - the safety argument: not relayed at destination time `t`, and `t` past the send time plus `EXPIRY_PERIOD`, means it can never be relayed;\n  - activation conditions.\n- **`interop/predeploys.md`, `L2ToL2CrossDomainMessenger`:**\n  - adds `sentMessageTimestamps`, `expiredMessages`, `expireMessage` and its invariants, and `EXPIRY_PERIOD` (8 days, at least the expiry window);\n  - rejects the `L2CrossDomainMessenger` and `L2ToL1MessagePasser` as message targets on send and relay;\n  - removes `resendMessage`.\n- **`interop/predeploys.md`, new `UndeliveredMessageExporter`** predeploy at `0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000030`.\n- **`interop/superchain-eth-bridge.md`:** `refundETH`, the `RefundETH` event, invariant iSEB-004 (refund only for expired sends, at most once) and assumption aSEB-004.\n- **`interop/derivation.md`:**\n  - a dependency set must not configure an expiry window above `EXPIRY_WINDOW` (7 days), and nodes and the proof program must reject one that does;\n  - the security note now points to message expiry instead of resending.\n- **Navigation:** linked from `SUMMARY.md` and the interop overview.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-08T01:53:00Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-05T01:17:23Z",
      "additions": 726,
      "deletions": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABL4fvIQ",
      "title": "zk: align ZK dispute game specs with the implementation",
      "author": "wwared",
      "number": 983,
      "body": "Brings the ZK dispute game specs in line with the monorepo implementation: fixes outdated contract details (game type, `SuperRootProof` encoding, verifier, OPCM config and validation, game mechanics), adds the public interface reference, rewrites migration around `upgrade()`/`migrate()`, documents the SP1 program structure and proof completeness, and adds an honest actors page. The ZK Fault Proof VM page is renamed to ZK Proof System (with a redirect), and the dispute game interface, portal and OPCM migrator pages get matching fixes.\n\nCloses ethereum-optimism/proofs-team#9. Commits are self-contained and can be reviewed one by one.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-30T23:31:53Z",
